From 7268353ab7aeb063cc81c58c5dabc99de821b8dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 16:12:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/54] kaiair: add PktR IPC (Cantelli power target) +
 regime-transition-aware view

Phase 2 (compute + display only, no scheduler actuation):

- pktr_ipc.h: pure-math IPC. cantelli_sigma_factor(beta)=sqrt(beta/(1-beta)),
  power_target_db = G + I_R + gamma + sigma*k(beta), and the dual
  max_tolerable_interference_db = S - gamma - sigma*k(beta) (E_max[I_R]).
  pktr_config{gamma_db, beta, ewma_c} carries the knobs (YAML wiring is T0.3).

- pktr_ipc_test.cpp: 8 GTest cases (Cantelli factor at beta 0.5/0.8/0.9/0.99,
  monotonicity, extreme-beta clamping, worked examples). All pass on hardware.

- kaiair_pktr_metrics_view: surface the IPC target Tier-A in SINR space (the
  unknown gain G cancels): required UL SINR = gamma + sigma*k, the TPC delta to
  current SINR, and E_max[I_R]. Two honesty fixes from the first hardware run:
  * Relabel NI/I_R/E_max as I+N (dBFS, relative), RSRP is dBFS per SCF-222, so
    NI is offset from absolute dBm by RX-chain calibration (cancels in the
    differential TPC loop; dBFS->dBm calibration tracked for absolute claims).
  * Regime-transition flag: when EWMA sigma exceeds link jitter (>6 dB) the
    variance is mean-lag-dominated during a fast I+N step, not steady-state
    jitter; suppress the (invalid, absurd) cushion/target for that interval
    instead of printing e.g. 265 dB. Threshold becomes a pktr_config knob in T0.3.

Verified on the ARA gNB container: pktr_ipc_test 8/8 + pktr_link_state_test pass.
